<Layout title="Studio" description="An independent creative practice by Will Simons, moving between code, objects, and shared experiences.">
  <section class="shell page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">Simons Development Labs / The practice</span><h1>A studio for<br /><em>following a thread.</em></h1><p>I’m Will Simons, a software engineer, solo founder, and maker based in San Francisco. I’m building skateboard.fyi, an independent archive and research platform for skateboard print culture.</p></section>
  <section class="shell studio-story"><img src="/attachments/scan117684.avif" alt="A photograph from Will’s personal archive" /><div><span class="eyebrow">Code, wood, paper, light</span><h2>Start with curiosity.<br />Make something real.</h2><p>Sometimes that means building an archive for skate magazines. Sometimes it means finding a piece of wood in the desert and turning it into a light.</p><p>I started skateboard.fyi in 2025 and began physical archival work that December. I develop the platform and the tools that turn magazine scans into searchable records.</p><p>The form changes. The impulse stays familiar: pay attention, try something, see what it makes possible.</p><p>My path has taken me through software at Glowforge, winters making things at Mars College in Bombay Beach, and back to San Francisco. This studio is a place to bring those experiences together.</p></div></section>
